format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: radioactivity

lesson why-nuclei-decay
title: Why do nuclei decay?
minutes: 5
xp: 50
teaches: u2-spontaneous
teaches: u2-random-single
teaches: u2-parent-daughter
relies_on: u1-stable-unstable
relies_on: u1-unstable-changes

description:
    Some nuclei change all by themselves, and nobody can say when. You will meet the parent and the daughter, and find out why this is a natural process.

cite ref-iaea-decay
supports: Radioactive decay is spontaneous; parent and daughter nuclides.

cite ref-iaea-glossary
supports: Radionuclide; what radioactive means.

cite ref-openstax-up3-ch10
supports: Radioactive decay is random for one nucleus and regular for many.

card c01
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l1-predict-alone
scored: 0

card c02
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Stable and unstable
figure: simple-stable-unstable
figure_at: 1

body:
    A stable nucleus can stay as it is. An unstable nucleus can change into another state. A nucleus that can change like this is called [[radioactivity|radioactive]].

card c03
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: It changes by itself
figure: parent-daughter
figure_at: 1

body:
    An unstable nucleus can change all by itself. Nobody has to push it. The nucleus that changes is the [[parent-nuclide|parent]]. The nucleus it becomes is the [[daughter-nuclide|daughter]]. The change gives off [[radiation]].

card c04
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l1-hotspot-change

card c05
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l1-tom-person

card c06
kind: teach
type: reveal
scored: 0
title: Left alone, it can still change
predicts: c01
figure: parent-daughter
figure_at: 1

body:
    An unstable nucleus can change all by itself, even when nobody does anything to it. It does not vanish. It turns into a different nucleus and gives off radiation.

card c07
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Random for one, regular for many
figure: random-one
figure_at: 2

body:
    You can know that a nucleus has a chance of changing. You cannot say when. Look at one nucleus and its moment is a surprise. A whole group is different, and you will see how in a later lesson.

